 "title": "Exopolysaccharides and Their Biological Properties",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around exopolysaccharides (EPSs), a method or tool with various biological properties. EPSs have been studied by several researchers, including Banerjee, Breierová, Cho, Grigorova, and Mahapatra. They have been found to have biocompatibility with MDCK cell lines and no antiproliferative activity with MCF-7 cell lines. EPSs also produce exopolysaccharides in several organisms, including Bacillus atrophaeus WYZ, Ganoderma applanatum, Lactobacillus keﬁranofaciens ZW3, Leuconostoc lactis KC117496, and Rhodotorula mucilaginosa CICC 33013. Additionally, EPSs have been characterized to have a spectrum that can be analyzed by FT-IR and have a synergistic effect with guar gum.",
